<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean Samsung Corp '96 net rises.</title>
<headline>S.Korean Samsung Corp '96 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>							 1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Net						43.54 vs     20.61</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	common shares				10    vs     10</p>
<p>	preferred shares			   11    vs     11</p>
<p>    Turnover				   24,131.75 vs 19,253.81</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				     656    vs    792</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			    60.47 vs     31.34</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (both gain)		 5.02 vs     16.23</p>
<p>NOTE - Samsung Corp is a foreign trading and construction the sharp rises in turnover and net profit were mostly due to its absorption of a sister construction firm at the end of 1995. Its share capital increased by 6.8 million shares to 70.54 million in 1996 due to rights offering.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
